x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Owen Muir, M.D. and Nursing Colleague Michelle Bernabe see the sites around the convention center.</figcaption></figure></div><p><a href=\"https://opmed.doximity.com/articles/the-disconnect\">The Disconnect</a></p><p>Previous columns are also available, including:</p><p><a href=\"https://opmed.doximity.com/articles/more-disclosures-please-a-call-for-action-for-psychiatrists-to-engage-with-industry\">More Disclosures Please</a></p><p>In 2019, I addressed NPD:</p><p><a href=\"https://opmed.doximity.com/articles/the-mental-illness-so-stigmatized-we-dare-not-speak-its-name\">Mental illness so stigmatized we dare not speak its name</a></p><p>And the 2018 classic:</p><p><a href=\"https://opmed.doximity.com/articles/clinicians-self-disclosure-of-mental-illness-and-burnout-can-be-the-key-to-hope-ba8dea71-7d88-4cae-bd56-d9b2938bf57d\">Clinicians’ self-disclosure of mental illness and burnout can be a source of hope</a></p><p>Thanks for reading.  And thanks to <span class=\"mention-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Moral Health&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:77106,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;pub&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.substack.com/pub/moralhealth&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://bucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2f672c3e-1261-4f60-b1c7-7db0be547281_1280x1280.png&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;a307ff47-b7a7-49ea-9edd-c8d61cd2cecd&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"MentionToDOM\"></span> for joining me!</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>","text":"Doximity has built a great product. And doximity dialer is also amazing.\n\nThey also have asked your author to write a review of the American Psychiatric Association annual meeting…with tremendous latitude. I have done so again, in a style more in keeping with Lobster Consideration than anything else. I’m grateful for the opportunity.\n\nOwen Muir, M.D. and Nursing Colleague Michelle Bernabe see the sites around the convention center.\n\nThe Disconnect\n\nPrevious columns are also available, including:\n\nMore Disclosures Please\n\nIn 2019, I addressed NPD:\n\nMental illness so stigmatized we dare not speak its name\n\nAnd the 2018 classic:\n\nClinicians’ self-disclosure of mental illness and burnout can be a source of hope\n\nThanks for reading. And thanks to for joining me!\n\nSubscribe now"}